GTLib.opo is very large already, so I don't plan to add very much, but I will
write programmes which needs GTLib.

Nevertheless I could imagine the following enhancements of GTLib:
- Ellipses, a x- and y-raidus enhanced gcircle-command
- procedures for OS-Calls, e.g. file-infos, play, serial settings etc.
- scalable objects/symbols like arrows, checkmarks.
- procedure for usage with a serial mouse

It would be great if someone could rewrite some functions in assembler to
speed slow routines up, for example sort: and gwprint: ...


